# Design Docs Are the Direction

`Design/*.md` is the source of truth for look, feel, and UX. Read the matching doc before any
player-visible work (UI, menus, environment, creatures, traps, VFX, fonts, audio).

| Topic | Doc |
| --- | --- |
| Art pillar ("Crystalline Ley-Line Arcana"), floor/wall/door tiles, ley-line grid states, trap concepts, defender constructs | `Design/General.md` |
| Biome × resident creature matrix (Gothic/Undead, Goblin Tunnels/Orcs, Fungal Warren/Spiders, Sunken Ruins/Evil Fairies), core loop (dig → breach → defend) | `Design/Creatures and style.md` |
| Title menu: idle geode core, per-option hover FX, click transitions | `Design/Start Screen.md` |
| Fonts: titles (Friz Quadrata / Cinzel / Percolator), telemetry (Orbitron / Rajdhani / Exo 2), body (Goudy Old Style / Palatino) | `Design/fonts.md` |
| LitRPG genre conventions and game-design takeaways (essence loop, reputation, companion, core stakes) | `Design/Overall.md` |
| Per-faction creature asset picks (base / medium / boss) and intruder heroes | `Design/Monsters.md` |

## Pillars to hold in mind

- Clean, not grimy: polished obsidian/amethyst floors, dark basalt walls pocketed with glowing quartz,
  sapphire, emerald geodes. No mud-and-torches dungeon dressing.
- Grid is visible through hair-thin fractures that pulse when a room is powered; zone state = line
  state (powered: bright/clean, dormant: dark/cracked, attacked: white-hot arcing).
- Breaching a biome swaps tile style in place; the core room always stays the clean obsidian style.
- Target layout is a 21:9 monitor; telemetry text prioritizes legibility over styling.

## Rules

- **`Design/Monsters.md`:** four tier **rows** per family (Worker / Minion / Elite / Boss) — see `monsters-tier-grid.mdc`; alternates go in the note cells.
- Implement what the doc says; if a doc is silent on the point you need, say so and state the assumption
  you are making rather than inventing direction silently.
- When a design decision is made in conversation, append it to the relevant `Design/*.md` in the same
  short, concrete style (colors, timings, asset ids, scale in UU).
- Translate described moods into `search_library.py` queries per `asset-library-first.mdc`
  (e.g. "basalt + geode" → `Crystal_Cave`, `Lost_Cave`; "ruined cathedral pillars" → `Gothic_Cathedral_5.4`).
